Validate t-digest images, and keep weighted means finite.

Found by data.sketches tools/fuzz under UBSan, the last on valid data too:

- The reference-implementation (compat) formats store k and the centroid
  weights as floating point, converted to integers unchecked: NaN or an
  out-of-range value is undefined behavior. k must now be in [10, 65535] and
  a weight at least 1 and within 64 bits.
- The weights, buffered values included, must sum without wrapping the
  64-bit total, and min <= max, with every buffered value in [min, max] and
  every centroid mean within a rounding margin of it.
- centroid::add() and weighted_average() multiplied a mean by a weight before
  dividing, and took differences of means of opposite sign: for values near
  the largest double both overflow, so a t-digest of finite data reported an
  Inf or NaN median and could not be read back after serializing. They now
  divide first, and fall back to the form whose terms cannot overflow.

